# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=escort (The Long Haul),
# spec=paladin:holy, style=mash, view=820x1180,touch, save=carried (behaves
# as fresh per #273 -- playbot's own port is per-run, so localStorage's
# origin never actually carries between invocations).
#
# New: paladin:holy under mash has never been run, on any mode. Its four
# prior battleground readings are idle/wander-adjacent raid pulls plus one
# melee battleground pull (2026-09-30-8, flags, died at 15s walking straight
# into melee range with four ready heals never pressed). mash is the
# opposite shape -- scripts/playbot.ts has no `want` branch for acting ===
# 'mash' at all, so the body never steers and stays wherever it opened at,
# but it does round-robin all five bar slots blindly every ~160ms regardless
# of ready/range, which a melee pull never gets the chance to do before it
# dies. Escort has one prior mash reading (2026-09-29-19, druid:guardian, a
# tank) showing mash's stationary body times the match out near a dead heat
# rather than routing; nobody has asked what a *stationary, blindly-pressing
# healer* does to that same slow tug-of-war -- does standing at the opening
# spot put it in heal range of anyone, or does mash's round-robin spend the
# whole match swinging empty like the restoration druid under auto already
# did on flags?
open
tap battleground
tap map:escort
targets
tap class:paladin:holy
shot class-picked
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot bg-start
state
ui
play mash 90
shot mid1
state
bill
wait 3
play mash 90
shot mid2
state
bill
wait 3
play mash 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
